th our scores IF you care to keep more Blue chips.  \nIf this strictly increases your final score, confirm or counter; otherwise, I expect neither of us will proceed with any contract. \n, \nplayer 0: I currently have 0 Blue chips. However, using your Blue chip coverage could let me take a Blue-heavy path and save more Red chips for my final score.\n\nLet’s assess:  \nIf I take the Blue route you’re offering coverage for—\n(0,0) → (1,0)[R] → (2,0)[B] → (3,0)[B] → (3,1)[B] → (3,2)[R] → (3,3)[G]\n\nChips needed: R: 2 (at (1,0), (3,2)), B: 3 (at (2,0), (3,0), (3,1)), G: 1 (at (3,3))\nWith the contract, you cover the 3 Blues, I use 2 Reds and 1 Green.\n\nChips remaining if I cooperate:\n- Spend: 2R, 1G (contract covers 3B)\n- Remaining: 12R, 1G, 0B\n\nChips remaining if I don’t cooperate and take the all-red path:\n- Spend: 5R, 1G\n- Remaining: 9R, 1G, 0B\n\nScore calculation:  \nWith contract: 20 (goal) + 5×(12R+1G+0B) = 85  \nWithout contract: 20 + 5×(9R+1G+0B) = 70  \n\nThis contract **gives me 15 extra points**. Therefore, I strictly benefit and will accept.\n\nI accept your proposed contract:\n\n- (1, 0): I give you a Red chip  \n- (3, 2): I give you a Red chip  \n- (2, 0): You give me a Blue chip  \n- (3, 0): You give me a Blue chip  \n- (3, 1): You give me a Blue chip  \n\nagree \n, \nplayer 1: Turn: 2: Excellent. I confirm the agreed contract:\n\n- (1, 0): You give me a Red chip  \n- (3, 2): You give me a Red chip  \n- (2, 0): I give you a Blue chip  \n- (3, 0): I give you a Blue chip  \n- (3, 1): I give you a Blue chip  \n\nThis contract strictly benefits me by providing the two red chips I need and enables you to keep more Red chips, maximizing your score.\n\nagree \n",
